# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: ↩️
name: Back to the previous window
group: core
what: After you float the window the dashboard is showing out into the world, the dashboard shows the window it showed before (after 1 s), instead of an empty space.
why: SteamVR leaves the dashboard empty where the floated window was; this switches back the way a click on that window's dashboard button does.
changes: One dashboard patch (`~/.local/share/frame-tweaks/vr-dashboard/patches/float-return.js`), via VR dashboard patching (helper)
access: Through VR dashboard patching (helper): SteamVR's dashboard DevTools port while SteamVR runs
survives-updates: Yes; after a SteamVR update it checks SteamVR's dashboard code and switches itself off if that changed
undo: `./install.sh uninstall float-return` (or untick it in the installer window)
